<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Papua New Guinea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Papua <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> is a country occupying the eastern half of the island of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and nearby islands in the south-western Pacific, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-moresby">Port Moresby</a>. Divided between British, later Australian, Papua and German New Guinea, it was administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and became independent on 16 September 1975. It is among the most linguistically diverse countries in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea.jpg" alt="Papua New Guinea" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Nightstallion · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Papua_New_Guinea.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
